When the task involves building a go-to-market context repository, distilling GTM dashboards
or strategy documents into a repo, logging a market signal, taking a periodic snapshot, or
producing or checking customer-facing copy against a brain, read `{{SKILL_PATH}}/SKILL.md`
first and follow its procedure.

It routes to three modes: BUILD a new brain, UPDATE one from a signal or snapshot, or OPERATE
it to produce and QA an asset. Load the reference file that SKILL.md names for the mode you
are in rather than improvising the method.

If a built brain exists here, its entry file and `rules/` layer load before any customer-facing
writing, and `ops/QA-checklist.md` runs before the draft comes back.
